{"entryId":"1710","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1710:1","sourceSha256":"078f4d42b3975d1b2bf64667e5166c3c9d111010223e6b1161312ec2354f88f0","englishSha256":"71c29b07a67d8be14128854912d59977fa3ab4256397373e41234223bf646b4b","citations":[{"id":"1710:1:citation-01","he":[18,148],"en":[97,109],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_45b.18"},"reference":"Berakhot 45b:18","assessment":"The direct passage has bare Yehudah bar Meremar, Rav Acha of Difti, and Mar bar Rav Ashi, with none outstanding over the others. They take the question to Meremar. Preserve the compiler’s reported fuller name and the distinction from Pappa.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 45b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_45b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1710:1:citation-02","he":[150,229],"en":[289,300],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_52b.18"},"reference":"Ketubot 52b:18","assessment":"Rav Pappa arranged a match for his son with Abba Sura’ah’s household and went to write the bride’s ketubah. Yehudah bar Meremar meets him at the door and Pappa invites him in.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 52b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_52b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1710:1:citation-03","he":[231,273],"en":[454,468],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_80b.1"},"reference":"Ketubot 80b:1","assessment":"The attribution from Rava is confirmed, with Pappa reporting a conflicting ruling from Rava and explaining that the first position was inferred.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 80b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_80b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 80b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_80b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2],"holds":[{"raw":"לפני רב פפא פ' ג' שאכלו","reason":"Prese